<i>
<p></p>
The Economic Stimulus Act of 2008, signed into law on
      February 13, raised the conforming loan limit through the end of
      2008 for a first mortgage on a single-family home in the
      contiguous United States from $417,000 to 125 percent of the
      median house price in certain high-cost areas, with an overall
      cap of $729,750.<a href="#fn2"><sup>2</sup></a><a name="fn2r"></a>
      Questions <b>13-15</b>
 ask about your bank&#8217;s
      past and expected securitizations with, or sales to, Fannie Mae
      and Freddie Mac (the GSEs) of mortgage loans that do not conform
      to previous loan size limits but do conform under the new limits
      (<b>conforming-jumbo</b>
 mortgage loans). 
        </i>
